{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1234934-inspirational-material","id":1234934,"title":"Inspirational Material","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-07-14T06:51:50-07:00","id":1234934,"title":"Inspirational Material","content":"First of all: I absolutely adore what is being done with 2ed, backed it the Minute I heard the KS was live.<br /> As I will be ST for the Geist venue on our forum game, I thought you cannot start soon enough to gather ideas.<br /> I wanted to know what material other than the one mentioned in the preview come to mind?<br /> I thought about the early Episodes of Bleach and Supernatural (Road Kill was the name of one particular episode, I believe), maybe some Ghostbusters, and Curiously the first half or so of Shaman King. I was given to understand ghost hunt would also fit the theme somewhat, though closer to Blue book mortals. Dresden Files might work when dealing with the Kenmlerites.<br /> I Personally feel like the Count of Monte Christo could work very well as a template for a vengeful Bound.<br /> What I am deeply missing, however, is stories about a malevolant plane like the Underworld. I know they exist, I have some that I half-remember, but nothing I can place right now.<br /> <br /> If you have any good ghost stories, blueprints for Geists, ghosts or sineaters (Danny Phantom? ^___^) or evil plane stuff, please share.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T07:00:54-07:00","id":1234936,"title":"","content":"Persona 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T09:04:56-07:00","id":1234978,"title":"","content":"All-New Ghost Rider and the other stories that feature Robbie Reyes as Ghost Rider apply, there is a bit of a Sin-Eater/Geist dynamic with him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T15:31:01-07:00","id":1235094,"title":"","content":"Beyond: Two Souls","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-14T17:11:47-07:00","id":1235111,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">One very worth mentioning that often gets overlooked:</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The 2015 anime</span></span></span><i> Death Parade</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> is about a judge in the afterlife, a &quot;bartender&quot; who runs parlor games for the recently deceased. By playing a game of billiards, darts, table hockey, arcade fighting, or even Twister, one person gets to be reincarnated while the other is sent to the void for annihilation. The ultimate theme (without spoiling too much) is about having compassion for the dead, which suits Geist 2e's themes rather well.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">The theme song is also a big party, which is appropriate. Nobody in this opening is a living human being.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=UjjTMNDZi-A\" data-code=\"UjjTMNDZi-A\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/UjjTMNDZi-A/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div></span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13580-hsienfan","name":"Hsienfan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13580_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T02:50:11-07:00","id":1235222,"title":"","content":"Haunt. Jaded priest who believes in nothing but loves his brother. His brother, a patriotic covert operative who dies. His ghost manages to stick around and help out his brother, and occasionally they merge forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-15T04:44:18-07:00","id":1235241,"title":"","content":"Ghost Whisperer could get very saccharine sometimes - though at other times, the lead character could really go through the wringer - but it was someone who could see and lay ghosts, and they knew it and wouldn't leave her alone. Also, the basement of her shop had a hole in the foundations that led to a buried and often ghost-filled former iteration of the town.<br /> <br /> Of all things, Pretty Little Liars does a good line in <i>secrets</i> (rather than ghosts - but there are enough long lost people who could be recast as ghosts) intruding on the present.<br /> <br /> On a darker note, Millennium is about a profiler who can see psychic echoes of crimes and other evils, which could also be recast as ghosts (and sometimes figuratively are within the show itself). Plus there are darker forces that could be reapers, chthonians, and other deathly monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T10:19:19-07:00","id":1235613,"title":"","content":"The movies &quot;Stir of Echoes&quot; and &quot;The Others&quot; could provide very good inspiration for Absent characters who are still coming to grip with &quot;reality&quot;. They are very different films but each is suspenseful in its own way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/693-thomasm","name":"ThomasM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar693_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"126"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T14:35:38-07:00","id":1235718,"title":"","content":"I hear from the Kickstarter Discussion that Cthonians are often fish-like. I wonder how much inspiration I can wring for them from the Korean webtoon Tower of God. (Last time I was still reading it, they had floating giant fish-things frequently in the eponymous tower)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-16T14:43:22-07:00","id":1235722,"title":"","content":"I think I will add Soul Reaver to my inspirational material: the whole feel of the Astral realm, the inhabitants dvouring souls, the idea of a consuming entity etc are not spot on, but feel close enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-25T11:40:06-07:00","id":1238640,"title":"","content":"Just re-watched the Twilight Zone episode &quot;Death's Head Revisited,&quot; and it basically plays out like a Geist story might, including examples of higher-level Memoria and Boneyard effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13641-mad_maudlin","name":"Mad_Maudlin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"229"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-26T15:38:18-07:00","id":1239056,"title":"","content":"The Underworld has reminded me of the Dark Souls series since I first read the preview of it on the Onyx Path blog. Both of their settings revolve around a fundamental entropy and tend toward desperation and corruption. They're both also filled with secrets whose uncovering require you to go out of your way and understand the world's specific rules and inclinations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24427-snazzerdoo","name":"Snazzerdoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-03T04:35:54-07:00","id":1242294,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=IkB6zaJnLj0\" target=\"_blank\">This Crypt TV shor</a>t feels like a reasonable plot hook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-04T11:33:56-07:00","id":1242760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=lPOM0IUsd_0\" data-code=\"lPOM0IUsd_0\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/lPOM0IUsd_0/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/2.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12708-chesh","name":"Chesh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12708_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"238"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-05T21:24:18-07:00","id":1243110,"title":"","content":"Shadow of Mordor is the best game and inspiration for Geist 2e, even though it's a fantasy. You have a Wraith (Geist) that possesses you and raises you from the dead every time and let you use his wide variety of powers that you unlock with choices in skill trees. I sometimes wonder if Shadow of Mordor was ripped off from Geist 1e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22337-overcastghost","name":"OvercastGhost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22337_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-25T20:53:47-07:00","id":1257298,"title":"","content":"As I've just watched Netflix's <b>Bleach</b>, I got some new interpretations on <b>Geist </b>matters of it... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:18px\"><b>Bleach</b></span><br /> The <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt0434665/?ref_=tt_rec_tt\" target=\"_blank\">original anime</a> and <a href=\"https://www.imdb.com/title/tt5979872/\" target=\"_blank\">Netflix's movie</a> ( surprising good adaptation, I may add ) can be seen as much lighter <b>Geist </b>game. If <a href=\"http://bleach.wikia.com/wiki/Shinigami\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Shinigami</i></a> ('Gods of Death') are <b>very</b> human looking Japanese going full samurai-style Reapers ( using Death Swords instead of Death Masks ) defending series Underworld ( <a href=\"http://bleach.wikia.com/wiki/Soul_Society\" target=\"_blank\">Soul Society</a> ) from dead running from it. Shinigami are also taking care that Underworld beings do crossing over and destroying Living World. Protagonist, Ichigo, is first Sin-Eater in this world as he is still living teenager that's survives his death and in Bound-like event becomes part time Shinigami ( so part Reaper ) - and by this is ostracized in Soul Society. And if you still wonder on this as <b>Geist</b> inspiration - just see those terrifying looking Chthonians ( <a href=\"http://bleach.wikia.com/wiki/Hollow\" target=\"_blank\">Hollows</a> ) attacking humans! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> ( Origins of those in <b>Bleach</b> is different than Chthonians from <b>Geist</b>, but just see those arts! )<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/Ewj2R95.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> </div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-27-2018, 12:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-30T11:22:05-07:00","id":1258232,"title":"","content":"Rewatched with my partner today...<br /> <br /> <b><b>Beetlejuice</b></b><br /> <br /> It's a more comedy than horror, but it has some cool <b>Geist</b> stuff. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Story is about young married couple of self-aware ghosts ( Rank 2 ). They beloved house ( being their Anchor ) is taken by new big city family that drives the dead crazy. They summon Absent from Underworld that is known from making humans run away and make a deal with him for the Essence. In the meantime, couple befriend daughter of new home owners that is medium ( some inspiration for Sin-Eaters here ). In the end married ghosts and teenager need to send Absent away, as he is more a problem than solver. In movie there is also interesting take on modern Underworld as civil services and very cool way to create Avernian Gates. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-30-2018, 02:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-12T17:47:21-07:00","id":1260376,"title":"","content":"The avatars from .Hack G.U. as geists and the AIDA as Cthonians.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1869-moonwolf8","name":"moonwolf8","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}